Subject: a member's figures tell its proposals refused and its redirects by cause and its parked publishes now with the oldest's age; a test build may plant refusals at the lead
Why: Quiver's three-machine lab (kiln's CP-T2.2 step 7; the publisher-after-kill plan, step 1) attributes each slow publish to its cause with the figures that show it: a leader's side of a stall needs its parked publishes' age and why its proposals and redirects went as they did. The member's clock for its parked publishes and its lead is the one its owner tells it, so a simulation's virtual time ages them. plant_refusals (mutants) is the plan's planted stall: every proposal refused, as the budget refuses one, for a window after the lead.

